  "description": "meme-id: farm_equipment_and_livestock_don_t_mix; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image juxtaposes a photo of a Black man and a white woman in an intimate, affectionate pose with the text 'farm equipment and livestock don't mix.' This creates a harmful and hateful stereotype by implying that the Black man is 'livestock' and the white woman is 'farm equipment,' suggesting he is an object to be used or controlled by her. This is a clear example of hypersexualization and racial stereotyping, portraying the Black man as inferior, animalistic, and subordinate to the white woman. The meme uses racist tropes to demean and dehumanize Black men, fitting the 'Anti-Black Stereotypes' category, specifically 'Hypersexualization' and 'Comparing Black people to primates' (by implying he is 'livestock'). The intent is to degrade and insult the Black man based on his race and gender, making it a hateful and harmful meme.",
